ga7X(){return"Ruler: tap the ruler button to place it. Move it with one finger (or press the pencil on its middle) and turn it with two (it rests every 15\xb0). While it is out, every pencil stroke is a straight line: started next to an edge it runs along that edge; elsewhere it runs parallel or square to the ruler when close to it, or straight in its own direction. The distance is shown as you draw.\n\nProtractor: a circular template. Move it with a finger or the pencil on its centre; pinch to resize, twist to turn its 0\xb0. A stroke started on its outer or inner edge follows the circle (arcs, showing the angle); a stroke started inside is a straight line at whole degrees.\n\nSnap to points: near an existing point, the new point jumps exactly onto it; an orange symbol and its name show which one.\n\n15\xb0 guides: while drawing a line close to a multiple of 15\xb0, it locks on and a dashed guide appears.\n\nExact measurements: tap roughly where the next point goes, type the length on the keypad and press Enter.\n\nImport: pictures, PDF (choose the scale it was drawn at, or calibrate with Scale) and DXF (exact lines and layers). They go on layers under your drawing; lower their opacity in the layers panel to trace over them."},
